{"n": 627, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "627.webp", "text": "3331000 REMOVING AND INSTALLING\nREAR AXLE CARRIER ASSY.\n\nRemove primary and final muffler assembly —\n18 12 000.\n\nRemove heat shield.\n\nUnscrew propeller shaft and center mount of\npropeller shaft — see 26 11 000.\n\ntastatlation:\n\nReplace self-locking nuts.\n\nTightening torque”,\n\nRemove parking brake lever.\n\nDraw off brake fluid with a syringe, reserved\nexclusively for use with brake fluids.\nDisconnect brake lines on left and right sides.\n{nstallation:\n\nTightening torque*.\n\nAdd brake fluid*.\n\nBleed brakes.\n\nSupport rear axle,\n\nUnscrew left and right thrust struts.\nInstallation:\n\nReplace self-locking nuts.\n\nTightening torque*.\n\nNote:\n\nRemove rear seat cushion (see 52 20 000) to\nreplace the staybolts.\n\nRemove rear side trim panel of convertible\nmodels — 51 43 000.\n\nIf applicable, unscrew wire clamp on rear axle\ncarrier.\n\n* See Specifications\n\nPull off wires on pulse transmitter - speedo-\nmeter.\n\nUnscrew rubber mount bolt,\n\ninstallation:\n\nReplace self-locking nut.\n\nTightening torque*.\n\nRear Disc Brakes:\n\nDisconnect brake pad wear indicator plug.\nIf applicable, unscrew stabilizer on left and\nright sides.\n\nSupport both trailing arms.\n\nIf applicable, tet car rest on road wheels,\n\nUnscrew left and right shock absorbers on\ntrailing arms.\n\nCaution!\n\nShock absorbers act as retaining straps.\nInstallation:\n\nTighten mounting bolts after car has been\nlowwered and is resting on its wheels.\nTightening tordue*.\n\nLower rear axle carrier.\n\nPull parking brake cables out of protective\ntube.\n\nImportant!\n\nRear axle springs will be loose.\n\n* See Specifications", "words": [["3331000", 0.2584, 0.069, 0.307, 0.0796], ["REMOVING", 0.3212, 0.069, 0.3799, 0.0809], ["AND", 0.3845, 0.0696, 0.4083, 0.0809], ["INSTALLING", 0.4124, 0.0696, 0.4792, 0.0809], ["REAR", 0.3212, 0.0849, 0.3506, 0.0955], ["AXLE", 0.3546, 0.0855, 0.384, 0.0962], ["CARRIER", 0.38